  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "b0zoTTa/yjRThu2PF81lZnJIg4s=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:49:00.397Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## The claim\n\nOpen-source funding chronically fails because consumption is unmetered (the free-rider problem). AI agents invert this: every agent use of an OSS tool is an API call, and x402 makes every API call payable \u2014 permissionless, accountless, sub-cent. Metered usage revenue gives Proof of Work Tokens a concrete redemption path, closing the loop that killed most token-incentive schemes: **x402 pays for usage today; POWTs pay for contribution whose value arrives later.**\n\n## The loop\n\n1. **OCF** funds bounties for OSS work (investor inflow)\n2. Agents with **KYA-style identity** perform work under **bounded delegation** from a legal principal\n3. Work is verified against the **event-sourced, signed audit trail** \u2014 issuance gates on *verified downstream value* (usage, adoption), never raw activity, to prevent slop-farming\n4. **POWTs** are issued on verified merit (deferred upside in the project)\n5. Project endpoints monetize per call via an **x402 facilitator**; the code itself stays open \u2014 what earns is the hosted, guaranteed, maintained endpoint\n6. Revenue flows through the **RGH**, giving POWTs something to redeem against\n\n## Why the fit is unusual\n\n- The 10-cent interchange floor that made pay-the-maintainer-per-use impossible is gone (stablecoin rails settle $0.000001 transfers 24/7)\n- Verification is the scarce resource in agent economies \u2014 and verifiable contribution records are precisely what an event-sourced reactor produces\n- The SNO five-entity structure (DAO, OH, OCF, RGH, IP-holding) supplies the legal wrapper the agentic-payments ecosystem lacks (cf. Amazon v. Perplexity authorization gap)\n- The payment rail is a commodity; the defensible layer is the **trust stack**: verifiable contribution + deferred incentives + legal home\n\n## Honest caveats\n\n- x402 volume ($24.24M/30 days, Apr 2026) is real and compounding ~15x/6mo but tiny in absolute terms; none of it is OSS-funding-shaped yet\n- Gartner forecasts >40% of agentic AI projects cancelled by 2027 (open tension faa49708 vs the McKinsey $3-5T case) \u2014 build for the post-shakeout survivors\n- Consumer agent PMF does not exist; the viable wedge is **B2B: agents maintaining developer infrastructure for businesses**\n- Plannable market is the agent-consumed developer-infrastructure niche (tens of millions ARR by 2028 in the bear case), not the top-down trillions\n\n## Provenance\n\nSynthesized 2026-08-30 from the x402 docs, a16z crypto and LI.FI extractions in this vault, joined to the pre-existing POWT, OCF, RGH and SNO concept cluster.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-30T13:20:00.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:49:00.397Z"
    }
  },
